    1550,
    425
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Vedanga Jyotisham (VJ) is the most ancient work on the",
   "bbox": [
    374,
    453,
    1550,
    494
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "discipline called Vedic astrology. This petite composition was",
   "bbox": [
    323,
    498,
    1549,
    547
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "sermonized by sage Lagadha about 3500 years ago in the",
   "bbox": [
    322,
    549,
    1550,
    596
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Vedanga period.",
   "bbox": [
    326,
    606,
    669,
    646
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The text of the work separately pertains to the Rigveda",
   "bbox": [
    397,
    651,
    1555,
    699
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "and Yajurveda, together is known as VJ.",
   "bbox": [
    324,
    705,
    1138,
    747
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The Atharva Jyotisha is entirely different, thus, not",
   "bbox": [
    400,
    752,
    1553,
    798
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "considered a part and parcel of the VJ.",
   "bbox": [
    321,
    804,
    1106,
    850
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "It was customary for Vedic Brahmanas to recite the text",
   "bbox": [
    400,
    854,
    1553,
    900
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "of VJ, once a day till the 20<sup>th</sup> century.",
   "bbox": [
    322,
    907,
    1074,
    948
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Like the Vedas, the work has been handed down through",
   "bbox": [
    402,
    974,
    1552,
    1012
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "oral transmission only.",
   "bbox": [
    324,
    1025,
    811,
    1064
   ]
  },
  {
